        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/f777123f-a3c7-42f5-a714-f3c173ef8552,1770417931005/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%28363%2C0%2C4896%2C2754%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Seen from the neck down, RCMP officers in red uniforms march on the street.' width='620' height='349' title='Royal Canadian Mounted Police (RCMP) cadets march at a graduation ceremony at the RCMP Academy, Depot Division in Regina, Saskatchewan, Canada, June 5, 2017.'/><p>A CBC investigation of RCMP disciplinary records reveals hundreds of cases of alleged gender-based violence by members. Through a series of access requests, CBC received more than 10 years of disciplinary allegations and outcomes. Experts fear the revelations are just the \u201ctip of the iceberg.\u201d</p>",
